    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `timezone` field is now derived from an owner's locality/region via a fixed IANA region-to-timezone table. Changes:\n\n1. **`Localities.java`** \u2014 added a pinned `REGION_TIMEZONE` map (`NSW\u2192Australia/Sydney`, `VIC\u2192Australia/Melbourne`, `QLD\u2192Australia/Brisbane`) and a `timezoneOfRegion(region)` lookup that returns `null` for unknown regions.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `timezone` mapping that feeds the existing region (`CustomerCode.regionOf(...)`, the same source as `locality`) into `Localities.timezoneOfRegion(...)`, so `locality` and `timezone` stay consistent.\n\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the new read-only `timezone` string property on the owner schema (the `OwnerDto` is generated from this spec at build time).\n\nResult: `AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsTimezoneForRegion` passes \u2014 an owner in Sydney (postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) reports `locality: \"NSW\"` and `timezone: \"Australia/Sydney\"` \u2014 and the full test suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
