    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing structure:\n\n- **Right unit.** `Localities` already owns the region-keyed reference tables (`REGION_POSTCODES`, the region/city maps). Adding `REGION_TIMEZONE` and `timezoneOfRegion(...)` there sits exactly alongside its siblings \u2014 same `Map.of` idiom, same \"pinned to match the acceptance spec\" doc-comment convention, same `null`-for-unknown contract as `postcodeRange`. A maintainer would look here first.\n- **Consistent wiring.** The new `@Mapping` mirrors the existing `locality`/`checkDigit` expression mappings, and it composes the two established helpers (`CustomerCode.regionOf` \u2192 `Localities.timezoneOfRegion`) rather than duplicating region logic. Deriving region from the customer code again (as `locality` already does) is inherent to MapStruct per-target expressions and matches the surrounding style \u2014 not new duplication worth refactoring.\n- **No catch-all growth.** One small focused method added; nothing is becoming a grab-bag.\n- **Spec fidelity in schema.** The openapi addition documents the derivation and the exact table, consistent with the neighboring `locality`/`customerCode` property docs.\n\nNo structural changes needed.",
